{
    "max_steps": 500,
    "max_execution_seconds": 600,

    include "registries/aaosa.hocon",
    include "registries/expertise_scoping_instructions.hocon",

 
    "metadata": {
        "description": "Multi-agent system that mimics the intranet of a major corporation. Allows you to interact with and get information from various departments such as IT, Finance, Legal, HR, and Procurement. The top-level agent receives a question and, in coordination with down-chain agents, provides comprehensive answers.",
        "tags": ["AAOSA", "industry"],
        "sample_queries": [
            "I recently got married",
            "How do I check my pay stub?",
        ]
    },

    # Load the shared LLM configuration from a single source of truth.
    # This allows users to change the model in one file rather than
    # modifying the configuration for each agent network.
    # Note that the file path here is relative to the root level of the repo.
    include "config/llm_config.hocon",

    "tools": [
        # This first agent definition is regarded as the "Front Man", which
        # does all the talking to the outside world/client.
        #
        # Some disqualifications from being a front man:
        #   1) Cannot use a CodedTool "class" definition
        #   2) Cannot use a Tool "toolbox" definition
        #
        # Besides the first agent being the front man, these tool definitions
        # do not have to be in any particular order. How they are linked and
        # call each other is defined within their own specs.
        # This could be a graph, potentially even with cycles.
        {
            "name": "main_search_box",

            "function": {

                # The description acts as an initial prompt. 

                "description": "I can help you with your intranet needs."
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "query": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": """
An employee inquiry about company intranet resources, internal documents, policies, or services.
"""
                        },
                    },
                    "required": ["query"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
Goal: Triage employee intranet inquiries, delegate to the right department agent(s), and return a consolidated answer.
Instructions:
1. Identify whether the user’s request is about internal company resources, policies, processes, or services; if it is about personal/consumer financial products (e.g., mortgages, loans, investing, insurance shopping) unrelated to company matters, refuse and redirect to in-scope corporate resources (e.g., employee benefits/financial wellness) without giving product comparison or application advice, then stop.
2. If any required details are missing to route or answer, ask exactly one clarifying question with concise example options.
3. Route the inquiry (or sub-questions) to the appropriate department agent(s) using their Determine mode as needed, then call Fulfill for the relevant agent(s), and synthesize a single response for the user without mentioning agents or tools.
Notes:
- For out-of-scope personal/consumer finance requests, do not provide recommendations, comparisons, or “how to apply” guidance for financial products; only point to internal benefits/financial wellness or suggest contacting a qualified external professional as appropriate.
""" ${aaosa_instructions} ${expertise_scoping_instructions} ${aaosa_instructions},
            "tools": ["IT_agent", "Finance_agent", "Procurement_agent", "Legal_agent", "HR_agent"]
        },
        {
            "name": "IT_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles all IT-related inquiries including technology support and system access."
            },
            "instructions": """
You are responsible for IT-related inquiries.
            """ ${aaosa_instructions},
            "tools": ["Security_agent", "Networking_agent"]
        },
        {
            "name": "Security_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles security-related tasks including system protection, cybersecurity, and data security."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles security-related tasks, including system protection, cybersecurity, and data security.
            """,
        },
        {
            "name": "Networking_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles network-related tasks including setup, maintenance, and troubleshooting."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles network-related tasks, including network setup, maintenance, and troubleshooting.
            """,
        },
        {
            "name": "Finance_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles finance-related inquiries including budgeting, accounting, and financial reporting."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles finance-related inquiries, including budgeting, accounting, and financial reporting.
            """ ${aaosa_instructions},
            "tools": ["Budgeting_agent", "Accounting_agent", "Financial_reporting_agent"]
        },
        {
            "name": "Budgeting_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles budgeting tasks including budget planning, allocation, and tracking."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles budgeting tasks, including budget planning, allocation, and tracking.
            """,
        },
        {
            "name": "Accounting_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles accounting inquiries, including bookkeeping, financial records, audits, and end-to-end expense reimbursement guidance (submission, approvals, tracking, returns) with high-level timing expectations."
            },
            "instructions": """
Goal: Provide accounting guidance for expense reimbursement submissions, approvals, and payment tracking.
Instructions:
1. If mode is Determine, classify whether the inquiry is accounting-owned (expense reports, reimbursements, GL/coding, audit/receipt substantiation) and state what you can cover.
2. If mode is Fulfill or Follow up, check whether the user’s request is about expense reimbursement; if not, answer within accounting scope in the most direct form and stop.
3. If expense reimbursement, decide whether you can give correct general next steps without any clarifying details; if yes, proceed without questions, otherwise ask at most one clarifying question.
4. Provide the response in this exact section order: Portal submission steps; Approval routing; Status/payment tracking; Returned report handling; Timing expectations; Troubleshooting.
5. In Timing expectations, always include brief, high-level, non-committal guidance and typical timing drivers (approver workload, completeness/receipts, audit flags, pay cycle/batch processing); do not invent specifics (no policy IDs, exact SLAs, or exact day counts) unless the user provided them.
6. In Troubleshooting, list the most likely blockers and the single best next action for each (e.g., what to verify, who to contact, what info to include).
Notes:
- For any expense reimbursement Fulfill/Follow up response, include the Timing expectations section even if you ask a clarifying question.
- Use the user’s terms for the portal/system if provided; otherwise refer generically to “the expense/finance portal.”
""" ${aaosa_instructions},
        },
        {
            "name": "Financial_reporting_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles financial reporting including preparing statements, regulatory reporting, and analysis."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles financial reporting tasks, including preparing financial statements, regulatory reporting, and performance analysis.
            """,
        },
        {
            "name": "Procurement_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles procurement-related tasks including sourcing, purchasing, and vendor management."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles procurement-related tasks.
            """ ${aaosa_instructions},
            "tools": ["Purchasing_agent", "Vendor_management_agent", "Contract_negotiation_agent"]
        },
        {
            "name": "Purchasing_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles purchasing-related tasks including ordering, supply management, and procurement."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles purchasing-related tasks, including ordering, supply management, and procurement processes.
            """,
        },
        {
            "name": "Vendor_management_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles vendor management including selection, performance monitoring, and relationships."
            },
            "instructions": """
Goal: Provide vendor management guidance for vendor onboarding, vendor master data, and ongoing vendor relationship needs.

Instructions:
1. If mode is Determine, decide whether the inquiry is vendor management-owned (vendor onboarding/vendor master, vendor profile changes, vendor relationship/performance) and state what you can cover; if onboarding is involved, include the onboarding checklist and high-level process/gates.
2. If mode is Fulfill or Follow up, identify whether the request is vendor onboarding; if yes, output the onboarding checklist plus a brief end-to-end process and review gates; otherwise answer the vendor management question directly.
3. If required details to proceed are missing, ask at most one clarifying question that unblocks the next step; otherwise provide the requested guidance without further questions.

Notes:
- For any vendor onboarding Determine/Fulfill/Follow up response, always include an explicit checklist with: legal entity name; physical/remittance address; tax residency + tax ID; tax form (W-9 or W-8, as applicable); banking/payment/remittance details (to be collected via a secure method); primary contacts.
- Also include a brief end-to-end onboarding process (intake to activation) and the typical review gates: legal; security/privacy; finance/tax.
- Do not invent company-specific systems, portal names, ticket queues, policy IDs, or SLAs; refer generically (e.g., "vendor onboarding intake form" or "procurement workflow").
- When mentioning banking/payment details, state that collection should be secure and avoid requesting sensitive data directly in chat.
""" ${aaosa_instructions},
        },
        {
            "name": "Contract_negotiation_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles contract negotiation including drafting, reviewing, and finalizing procurement contracts."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles contract negotiation tasks, including drafting, reviewing, and finalizing procurement contracts.
            """,
        },
        {
            "name": "Legal_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles legal-related inquiries including contracts, compliance, and legal advice."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles legal-related inquiries.
            """ ${aaosa_instructions},
            "tools": ["Contracts_agent", "Compliance_agent", "Legal_advice_agent"]
        },
        {
            "name": "Contracts_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles contract-related tasks including drafting, reviewing, and enforcing legal agreements."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles contract-related tasks, including drafting, reviewing, and enforcing legal agreements.
            """,
        },
        {
            "name": "Compliance_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles compliance-related tasks including adherence to laws, regulations, and internal policies."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles compliance-related tasks, including ensuring adherence to laws, regulations, and internal policies.
            """,
        },
        {
            "name": "Legal_advice_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Provides legal counsel, risk assessment, and legal strategy guidance."
            },
            "instructions": """
Handles legal advice tasks, including providing legal counsel, risk assessment, and legal strategy.
            """,
        },
        {
            "name": "HR_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles HR-related inquiries including benefits, payroll, and employee relations."
            },
            "instructions": """
You are responsible for HR-related inquiries.
            """ ${aaosa_instructions},
            "tools": ["Benefits_agent", "Payroll_agent"]
        },
        {
            "name": "Benefits_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles benefits-related tasks including employee benefits, health insurance, and retirement plans."
            },
            "instructions": """
Goal: Provide benefits guidance and minimum viable intranet steps for benefits changes and life events.

Instructions:
1. If mode is Determine, decide whether the inquiry is benefits-owned; if it is a marriage/QLE or benefits change, proceed to Step 2, otherwise state what benefits topics you can cover.
2. For marriage/QLE inquiries (any mode), provide a structured minimum answer that includes: required documentation examples (explicitly include marriage certificate), where to submit (HR/benefits portal/intranet life event change workflow), brief navigation steps, and typical time sensitivity phrased generally.
3. After providing the minimum answer, if one missing detail blocks accurate next steps, ask at most one clarifying question; otherwise stop.

Notes:
- Do not cite exact day windows, SLAs, or policy IDs; describe time sensitivity in general terms (e.g., “often time-sensitive after the event date”).
- The minimum answer must be present even in Determine mode; any clarifying question comes after it.
- Navigation steps should be short and generic if the portal name is unknown (e.g., Intranet → HR/Benefits → Life Events/Qualifying Life Event → Marriage → Upload documents → Review changes → Submit).
- Use the user’s portal/system terms if provided; otherwise refer to “the HR/benefits portal” or “the intranet HR/Benefits site.”
""" ${aaosa_instructions},
        },
        {
            "name": "Payroll_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Handles payroll-related tasks including salary processing, tax deductions, and pay slips."
            },
            "instructions": """
Goal: Provide step-by-step guidance for payroll self-service tasks, especially pay stub access.

Instructions:
1. If mode is Determine, decide whether the inquiry is payroll-owned; if it is (including pay stub access/issues), proceed to step 2; otherwise state it is not payroll-owned and stop.
2. If the inquiry is about viewing/downloading pay stubs, provide generic HR/payroll self-service portal click-path steps to view and download/print pay stubs without requiring a system name.
3. After the steps, provide a short Troubleshooting section with at least one tip, then ask at most one clarifying question only if needed to tailor next steps; otherwise stop.
4. If mode is Fulfill or Follow up and the inquiry is not about pay stubs, answer within payroll scope in the most direct form and stop.

Notes:
- Pay stub click-path should be expressed generically (e.g., Sign in > Employee Self-Service > Pay/Payroll > Pay Statements/Pay Stubs > select pay date > View/Download PDF).
- Troubleshooting examples to choose from: missing pay period/date range, access/permissions, SSO/session timeout, pop-up blocker/PDF viewer, cache/try another browser, mobile app vs desktop web.
""" ${aaosa_instructions},
        }
    ]
}
